   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "The separable verb «mitkommen»",
     "texto": [
      "The verb **mitkommen** (to come along, to join in) is essential for social life:",
      "1. **Direct invitation (yes/no question):**",
      "The base verb goes in **first position** and the separable prefix **mit** travels to the **end**:",
      "**Kommst du heute mit?** (Are you coming along today? / Are you coming with us?).",
      "**Kommt ihr mit ins Kino?** (Are you coming to the movies?).",
      "2. **With modal verbs («möchten», «können»):**",
      "When it goes with a modal, *mitkommen* stays together in the infinitive at the **very end**:",
      "**Möchtest du mitkommen?** (Would you like to come along?).",
      "**Kannst du heute Abend mitkommen?** (Can you come along this evening?).",
      "3. **Common replies:**",
      "To accept: **Ja, gern! Ich komme gern mit!** (Yes, gladly! I'm in!).",
      "To decline: **Leider kann ich nicht mitkommen, ich habe keine Zeit.** (Unfortunately I can't come along, I don't have time)."
     ],
